@startuml
title SEQ-06 - AI Reading Preview, Publication and Quiz
autonumber
actor User
boundary Web
control GotIt
control Core
participant AI as "Configured Reading Provider"
database DB as "product_gotit"

User -> Web: Configure topic/language/level/type/length/items
Web -> GotIt: GET /reading/quota
GotIt -> Core: Authenticate + reading.ai entitlement
GotIt -> DB: Read quota bucket
GotIt --> Web: limit/used/remaining/reset
User -> Web: Generate
Web -> GotIt: POST /reading/preview
GotIt -> DB: Reserve quota atomically
GotIt -> DB: Resolve owned explicit/smart target items
GotIt -> AI: Structured generation\nUntrusted topic and target meanings
AI --> GotIt: title + bodyText
GotIt -> GotIt: Validate length/schema and bind exact target ranges
alt Missing targets
  GotIt -> AI: One bounded repair with previous draft + missing targets
  AI --> GotIt: repaired draft
  GotIt -> GotIt: Validate or deterministic salvage/bind
end
alt Generation fails
  GotIt -> DB: Release quota reservation
  GotIt --> Web: Safe provider error
else Valid preview
  GotIt -> GotIt: Create signed/encrypted publication token
  GotIt --> Web: preview + targets + token
end
Web --> User: Show unpublished preview
User -> Web: Open/save reading
Web -> GotIt: POST /reading\nIdempotency-Key + publicationToken
critical Publish or replay
  GotIt -> GotIt: Verify token scope/expiry/snapshots
  GotIt -> DB: Insert generated_content + target bindings + receipt
end
GotIt --> Web: Opened reading
opt Article quiz
  Web -> GotIt: Create article_quiz practice session
  GotIt -> DB: Bind exercises to reading targets
  GotIt --> Web: Server-scored quiz flow
end
note over Web,DB
Preview alone is not persisted as opened content and grants no learning evidence.
Only scored quiz attempts affect learning.
end note
@enduml

